create application for true color ansi terminal (linux based) using UTF-8 character set. Application should be able to use ffmpeg and
  gstreamer to play suppored audio files (mp3, flac,...) and during play should show small text based UI showing frequency bars using fast
  fourier transformation. It should use known UTF-8 characters for play, stop, pause, next song, previous song. Characters (buttons)
  should be mapped to space (play/pause) '<' (previous song), '>' (next song) and 's' or 'S' for stop. These buttons should also react on
  mouse click. Look and feel similar to application bpytop. Layout of text UI: 10 characters tall for frequency spectrometer. 1 character
  tall under for 4 buttons (aligned to center). Frequency spectrometer should be 20 characters wide. It sould be written in C++ compilable
  under ubuntu 24.04lts and use ncurses (or any similar). The spectrometer should be able to refresh itself up to 100ms.
